sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design (agreed with Nick, 2026-11-07): each task VM host keeps one stopped base VM, `shark-base`, that never gets an identity. Its ZFS snapshot is the base a task start copies; there is no Incus image and no publish. After a release, and daily, the base VM converges and a new snapshot becomes the base, so a task start's converge stays near a no-op.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: none · after a release, and daily
  %% kind: task_vm.image_refresh
  autonumber
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane H icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  %% lane VM icon=server pill=base VM tone=purple
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant H as Task VM host<br/>Incus over ssh
  participant VM as Base VM<br/>shark-base
  Note over GW: Admit the refresh<br/>one run per host
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-task-vm-image-refresh
  SW->>H: Start the base VM<br/>incus start
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - starts the stopped base VM; about 10 s to its guest agent; its containers start with it
  %%> - a host without a base VM gets it here, once: `incus init` from the stock Ubuntu VM image that `task-vms:prepare-host` copied, an empty seed volume, and a first boot that makes the `orbit` account with the key of the Swamp control Node and installs the SSH server; the converge builds everything else
  %%> - the task VM project keeps `restricted.snapshots=allow`: the base is a snapshot, and only a host API client can take one
  SW->>VM: Converge<br/>the same converge as a task start
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - each part runs only when its digest changed: the outer VM, the warm checkout at the release commit, each container
  %%> - no wait for the nested Gateway and no identity wipe: the base VM never gets an identity, and readiness belongs to a task start
  SW->>H: Stop and snapshot<br/>VM and seed
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - stops the base VM and snapshots it and its seed volume under the run's name; ZFS snapshots, about 1 s
  SW->>H: Prove the candidate<br/>one task start
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - steps 2 to 4 of a task start from the new snapshot in a free slot, then its release
  SW->>H: Prune old snapshots<br/>keep -previous
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - keeps the new snapshot and the one before it; removes older ones of the VM and the seed
  alt the run passes
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>new snapshot
    Note over GW: Promote<br/>record the new snapshot
    %%> Result:
    %%> - task starts copy the new snapshot; the one before it is `-previous`
    %%> - target: about 25 s for a no-op refresh before the proof (boot 10 s, converge 8 s, stop 5 s, snapshot 1 s); the first refresh of a new host builds the whole base, so it takes much longer
  else a step failed
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>failed step
    %%> On failure:
    %%> - the base VM is stopped and rolled back to the recorded snapshot, and a new snapshot is removed; task starts keep the recorded one
  end
